{"data":[{"category":"Other","cluster_posts_results":[{"post_id":"2108679039850557934"},{"post_id":"2108650796803883335"},{"post_id":"2108681908926165154"},{"post_id":"2108675158483612158"},{"post_id":"2108648513294737467"},{"post_id":"2108653143340839387"},{"post_id":"2108677940712276271"},{"post_id":"2108680470359662926"},{"post_id":"2108685198233891155"},{"post_id":"2108658844930900258"}],"contexts":{"topics":["News"]},"disclaimer":"This story is a summary of posts on X and may evolve over time. Grok can make mistakes, verify its outputs.","id":"2108723656566149535","name":"MTN Nigeria Customers Report Widespread Internet and Network Disruptions","summary":"Numerous users in Nigeria complained about MTN Nigeria's unreliable internet service, network outages, failed data purchases, and subscription issues. MTN customer support responded to affected users by requesting details via direct messages for investigation and resolution. Similar disruptions were reported with Airtel, leading to calls for refunds and service improvements.","updated_at":"2026-10-10T01:14:25.000Z","url":"https://x.com/i/trending/2108723656566149535"},{"category":"News","cluster_posts_results":[{"post_id":"2108443597225840789"},{"post_id":"2108523946484072549"},{"post_id":"2108493242924679383"},{"post_id":"2108482342524514424"},{"post_id":"2108531725819338824"},{"post_id":"2108484571306373365"},{"post_id":"2108482607902027994"},{"post_id":"2108478958752649275"},{"post_id":"2108551984131223850"},{"post_id":"2108500275342245923"}],"contexts":{"topics":["News"]},"disclaimer":"This story is a summary of posts on X and may evolve over time. Grok can make mistakes, verify its outputs.","id":"2108554715374268858","name":"Widespread Network Outages Disrupt MTN, Airtel, and Glo Services in Nigeria","summary":"Users across Nigeria reported severe internet and network disruptions starting with MTN and extending to Airtel and Glo, preventing access to data, calls, and USSD services. Network providers including MTN Nigeria and Airtel Nigeria responded on social media by requesting affected numbers via direct messages for assistance and raising support tickets.","updated_at":"2026-10-09T14:02:45.000Z","url":"https://x.com/i/trending/2108554715374268858"},{"category":"News","cluster_posts_results":[{"post_id":"2108254954406457696"},{"post_id":"2108274632205754490"},{"post_id":"2108260056290746753"},{"post_id":"2108286177300074675"},{"post_id":"2108288745304633389"},{"post_id":"2108254954406457696"},{"post_id":"2108233952138051924"},{"post_id":"2108256940052902194"},{"post_id":"2108355314323968066"},{"post_id":"2108580612856848632"}],"contexts":{"topics":["Business & Finance"]},"disclaimer":"This story is a summary of posts on X and may evolve over time. Grok can make mistakes, verify its outputs.","hook":"Customers in Lagos and beyond stared at blank screens on October 8, 2026, as MTN's FibreX broadband vanished while mobile hotspots barely kept them connected.","id":"2108226304273162604","name":"MTN Nigeria Faces Major Outage Across Multiple States","summary":"Widespread service disruptions hit MTN Nigeria users in Lagos, Oyo, Rivers, Delta, and the Federal Capital Territory, knocking out voice calls, data, and FibreX fixed broadband. Frustrated customers shared stories of missed work deals and constant restarts, with some turning to competitors' hotspots that also faltered. MTN acknowledged the downtime, blamed possible high temperatures at a data centre, and had engineers racing to restore services amid ongoing complaints.","updated_at":"2026-10-09T06:28:05.000Z","url":"https://x.com/i/trending/2108226304273162604"},{"category":"Other","cluster_posts_results":[{"post_id":"2108494970512695431"},{"post_id":"2108527996294312127"},{"post_id":"2108554804738040063"},{"post_id":"2108570475601564062"},{"post_id":"2108533381478678714"},{"post_id":"2108587194034122947"},{"post_id":"2108562420255875572"},{"post_id":"2108562251087020432"},{"post_id":"2108607806060278217"},{"post_id":"2108534264006324356"}],"contexts":{"topics":["News"]},"disclaimer":"This story is a summary of posts on X and may evolve over time. Grok can make mistakes, verify its outputs.","id":"2108590709553189170","name":"Viral Tweet from Chad Sparks Widespread Surprise and Discussion on X About Internet Access in Chad","summary":"A tweet from Chad prompted numerous reactions on X, with users expressing shock at seeing content from a Chadian for the first time. Discussions highlighted perceptions of limited internet access in Chad, featuring jokes comparing it to public phones or government offices only. Users from Kenya and Nigeria engaged heavily, contrasting Chad's connectivity with their own experiences involving generator noise and power issues.","updated_at":"2026-10-09T19:17:16.000Z","url":"https://x.com/i/trending/2108590709553189170"},{"category":"News","cluster_posts_results":[{"post_id":"2108614107477729559"},{"post_id":"2108593177670328541"},{"post_id":"2108625770059092271"},{"post_id":"2108621822132687184"},{"post_id":"2108630704255057923"},{"post_id":"2108636042572255743"},{"post_id":"2108602582520520820"},{"post_id":"2108651019106500712"},{"post_id":"2108602571715989670"},{"post_id":"2108614743460294940"}],"contexts":{"topics":["News","Politics"]},"disclaimer":"This story is a summary of posts on X and may evolve over time. Grok can make mistakes, verify its outputs.","id":"2108672568806736192","name":"Indian influencers Dhruv Rathee and Joydas warn protesters against using Bluetooth-based apps Bridgefy and Briar during internet blackout","summary":"Influencers Dhruv Rathee and Joydas advised protesters in India not to download or use Bluetooth-based apps Bridgefy and Briar, which enable communication via Bluetooth networks during internet blackouts. They stated these apps would undermine the purpose of the internet restrictions imposed amid protests. Warnings also extended to similar offline apps like Bitchat.","updated_at":"2026-10-09T23:03:11.000Z","url":"https://x.com/i/trending/2108672568806736192"},{"category":"News","cluster_posts_results":[{"post_id":"2108263646409466352"},{"post_id":"2108341038628921748"},{"post_id":"2108352605999202321"},{"post_id":"2108396011500843135"},{"post_id":"2108407593161175256"},{"post_id":"2108263646409466352"},{"post_id":"2108554265237274739"},{"post_id":"2108341038628921748"},{"post_id":"2108426393130500179"},{"post_id":"2108492538533523521"}],"contexts":{"topics":["Technology"]},"disclaimer":"This story is a summary of posts on X and may evolve over time. Grok can make mistakes, verify its outputs.","hook":"Orkut Buyukkokten remembers the days when social networks built real communities through scraps and testimonials. Now he's asking fans to sign up at orkut.com to bring that spirit back.","id":"2108403615690080331","name":"Orkut Founder Calls for Revival of Early Internet Friendships","summary":"The Turkish engineer who launched Orkut in 2004 shared a post inviting people to join a campaign for a new platform focused on genuine friendships and belonging, without algorithmic feeds. Supporters enter their email and country to get a personalized digital card with a unique code, then share it to rally others—over 255,000 have signed up so far, especially from India and Brazil where the original thrived until Google closed it in 2014. Fans like Paytm's Vijay Shekhar Sharma and others are posting their cards with excitement, though some wonder if it will lead to a full relaunch.","updated_at":"2026-10-09T06:45:32.000Z","url":"https://x.com/i/trending/2108403615690080331"},{"category":"News","cluster_posts_results":[{"post_id":"2108271211537191303"},{"post_id":"2102143223724392834"},{"post_id":"2108252329921118579"},{"post_id":"2108293864746574190"},{"post_id":"2108302479377265084"},{"post_id":"2108271211537191303"},{"post_id":"2108252329921118579"},{"post_id":"2108375540759499192"},{"post_id":"2108293864746574190"},{"post_id":"2108291678482383333"}],"contexts":{"topics":["Health & Fitness"]},"disclaimer":"This story is a summary of posts on X and may evolve over time. Grok can make mistakes, verify its outputs.","hook":"HHS Secretary Robert F. Kennedy Jr. is calling on Americans to share their stories about wireless tech's health impacts, from cell phones to 5G towers.","id":"2108295762291687866","name":"RFK Jr. Seeks Public Input on Wireless Radiation Health Effects","summary":"The Department of Health and Human Services launched a Request for Information on electromagnetic fields and radiofrequency radiation from devices like Wi-Fi, smart meters, and cell phones. It invites personal health experiences, clinical observations, research data, and thoughts on safety standards, with a focus on children and vulnerable groups—comments are due October 21 via regulations.gov under docket HHS-OASH-2026-0397. Officials aim to review science, compare global approaches, and shape policy, as Kennedy noted wireless tech is everywhere and science must catch up. Hundreds of responses have poured in already, reflecting both support for scrutiny and some skepticism.","updated_at":"2026-10-09T02:18:25.000Z","url":"https://x.com/i/trending/2108295762291687866"},{"category":"Other","cluster_posts_results":[{"post_id":"2107841294131220670"},{"post_id":"2107953700564357409"},{"post_id":"2107958273609523215"},{"post_id":"2107941752715751849"},{"post_id":"2107841294131220670"},{"post_id":"2107941752715751849"},{"post_id":"2107953700564357409"},{"post_id":"2107893155916091795"},{"post_id":"2107943505607721468"},{"post_id":"2107898287995195551"}],"contexts":{"topics":["Relationships"]},"disclaimer":"This story is a summary of posts on X and may evolve over time. Grok can make mistakes, verify its outputs.","hook":"A simple post captured how a stranger on the internet can slip into your daily routine, drawing thousands sharing their own heartfelt stories of quiet online bonds.","id":"2107971933812007199","name":"Online Strangers Become Part of Daily Routines","summary":"On October 7, @misak1nz wrote, 'And suddenly a stranger on the internet became a part of my daily routine,' sparking tens of thousands of likes and replies about 'oomfs'—affectionate shorthand for online mutuals or followers. Users shared warmth, like calling oomfs family or little ones they care for deeply, while some admitted shyness in interacting. The responses highlight how these digital connections offer real companionship, even as they note the ache when bonds fade, turning the moment into gratitude for screen-based communities.","updated_at":"2026-10-07T23:19:29.000Z","url":"https://x.com/i/trending/2107971933812007199"},{"category":"Other","cluster_posts_results":[{"post_id":"2108369472398692792"},{"post_id":"2108410025123381738"},{"post_id":"2108417338546745655"},{"post_id":"2108458737010893083"},{"post_id":"2108438803673477540"},{"post_id":"2108405871294423469"},{"post_id":"2108413578323874259"},{"post_id":"2108422691136917905"},{"post_id":"2108429263913275765"},{"post_id":"2108454934899519652"}],"contexts":{"topics":["Celebrity"]},"disclaimer":"This story is a summary of posts on X and may evolve over time. Grok can make mistakes, verify its outputs.","id":"2108481696630968339","name":"Janhavi Kapoor Posts Poll on X Asking Followers to Choose Between Starlink and Indian Telecom Brands Jio, Airtel, and Vi","summary":"Janhavi Kapoor posted a poll on X asking users to choose between Starlink and Indian telecom brands Jio, Airtel, and Vi. The poll sparked online debate on service quality, competition, data security, and compliance with Indian laws.","updated_at":"2026-10-09T08:59:32.000Z","url":"https://x.com/i/trending/2108481696630968339"},{"category":"Entertainment","cluster_posts_results":[{"post_id":"2108561901961597355"},{"post_id":"2108580559802794483"},{"post_id":"2108595831863455961"},{"post_id":"2108574972247748753"},{"post_id":"2108648253960982708"},{"post_id":"2108575528798302317"},{"post_id":"2108594877886017979"},{"post_id":"2108664262591656339"},{"post_id":"2108633314676359632"},{"post_id":"2108642406061265061"}],"contexts":{"topics":["K-pop"]},"disclaimer":"This story is a summary of posts on X and may evolve over time. Grok can make mistakes, verify its outputs.","id":"2108600786401820974","name":"Unknown Party Updates Loona Official Website Domain with Message Referencing All Twelve Members and Signed by Orbit","summary":"An unknown party acquired the domain for Loona's official website and updated it with a message stating, 'Twelve girls have gathered and created something beautiful. Even if we are apart or walk different paths, twelve places will still remain in our hearts under the same moonlight - Orbit.' The new site incorporates details from the group's lore, including a font created by member Heejin, members' representative colors, and shapes.","updated_at":"2026-10-09T22:39:20.000Z","url":"https://x.com/i/trending/2108600786401820974"},{"category":"News","cluster_posts_results":[{"post_id":"2108324128050864178"},{"post_id":"2108337600079810945"},{"post_id":"2108335265706115483"},{"post_id":"2108352695400546567"},{"post_id":"2108324128050864178"},{"post_id":"2108337600079810945"},{"post_id":"2108335265706115483"},{"post_id":"2108416881749303687"},{"post_id":"2108508663920971955"},{"post_id":"2108554891304349898"}],"contexts":{"topics":["Technology"]},"disclaimer":"This story is a summary of posts on X and may evolve over time. Grok can make mistakes, verify its outputs.","hook":"Imagine governments peering into your private thoughts for criminal cases. UN Secretary-General António Guterres raised this chilling possibility in a new report.","id":"2108368897875624255","name":"UN Warns Neurotech Could Let Governments Read Minds","summary":"Guterres highlighted risks of neurotechnologies expanding into justice systems, potentially enabling mind-reading, thought-based arrests, or mental state alterations without consent. He called for strict regulations treating thoughts as sensitive data under international law. People reacted with alarm, drawing parallels to *Minority Report* and Orwell's dystopias, while some noted current tech like fMRI falls short and voluntary AI data-sharing already exposes inner worlds.","updated_at":"2026-10-09T06:45:14.000Z","url":"https://x.com/i/trending/2108368897875624255"},{"category":"Other","cluster_posts_results":[{"post_id":"2108548221392056621"},{"post_id":"2108593573482680407"},{"post_id":"2108633173764821300"},{"post_id":"2108596768732492147"},{"post_id":"2108610795898655083"},{"post_id":"2108601347394429024"},{"post_id":"2108610670577226136"},{"post_id":"2108590269805294052"},{"post_id":"2108621205888729323"},{"post_id":"2108586795629965428"}],"contexts":{"topics":["News","Politics"]},"disclaimer":"This story is a summary of posts on X and may evolve over time. Grok can make mistakes, verify its outputs.","id":"2108636437834780928","name":"Indian social media user Priya advocates boycotting American apps in favor of Indian alternatives like Arattai, iBharat, MapmyIndia, Ulaa Browser, and AtoPlay","summary":"Priya (@LoopandPixels) posted on social media calling on Indians to boycott American apps such as WhatsApp, Google, Maps, Chrome, and YouTube. She recommended Indian alternatives including Arattai, iBharat, MapmyIndia, Ulaa Browser, and AtoPlay. The post sparked debate among users.","updated_at":"2026-10-09T19:17:27.000Z","url":"https://x.com/i/trending/2108636437834780928"},{"category":"Other","cluster_posts_results":[{"post_id":"2107900093193924930"},{"post_id":"2107900766166163732"},{"post_id":"2107900123158323335"},{"post_id":"2107900647559548990"},{"post_id":"2107917558041170390"},{"post_id":"2108513845438300312"},{"post_id":"2107900093193924930"},{"post_id":"2108512901283893657"},{"post_id":"2107900237042123198"},{"post_id":"2108512825887121603"}],"contexts":{"topics":["Art"]},"disclaimer":"This story is a summary of posts on X and may evolve over time. Grok can make mistakes, verify its outputs.","hook":"Just as excitement builds for the real ITIA Genesis drop, scammers rushed in with a phony collection promising mints at a $64.71 floor price.","id":"2107955611602194798","name":"IThinkItsArt Community Warns of Fake Genesis NFT Scam on OpenSea","summary":"On October 7, 2026, IThinkItsArt ambassadors like DOWNLOAD, sqr, and Lira quickly posted scam alerts, urging everyone not to connect wallets or buy from the fake OpenSea listing. They shared screenshots stamped 'FAKE' and stressed trusting only the official @IThinkItsArt account, with founders confirming all real Genesis news comes from there. The community rallied with protective messages like 'Protect the family' and even a Wayne's World GIF to vent frustration, keeping vigilance high ahead of the actual launch teased as 'GENESIS IS COMING.'","updated_at":"2026-10-07T22:13:30.000Z","url":"https://x.com/i/trending/2107955611602194798"},{"category":"Entertainment","cluster_posts_results":[{"post_id":"2107937584051875909"},{"post_id":"2107891182223405314"},{"post_id":"2108068628793082338"},{"post_id":"2108081845938360491"},{"post_id":"2108098852121452627"},{"post_id":"2107937584051875909"},{"post_id":"2108068628793082338"},{"post_id":"2108010732411326821"},{"post_id":"2107891182223405314"},{"post_id":"2108081845938360491"}],"contexts":{"topics":["Gaming"]},"disclaimer":"This story is a summary of posts on X and may evolve over time. Grok can make mistakes, verify its outputs.","hook":"Imagine firing up Black Ops 1 Zombies in a browser tab, no install needed—just Kino der Toten and Nacht der Untoten ready to go. Fans are reliving those endless rounds from 2010 with a simple link.","id":"2107945115671048448","name":"Classic Games Like Black Ops Zombies Now Play in Browsers","summary":"A fan decompilation project lets anyone play all original Black Ops Zombies maps plus DLC right in web browsers like vel.gg/bo1z, complete with Mystery Box spins and Pack-a-Punch upgrades. Skate 3 joins the fun too, thanks to 18-year-old developer Asher, running smooth at 360fps on phones, tablets, or PCs with multiplayer support. Nostalgia hits hard as players share grids of browser ports for Halo, Modern Warfare 2, and more, though some warn of malware risks from unknown sites and note companies have shut down similar efforts before.","updated_at":"2026-10-09T06:27:36.000Z","url":"https://x.com/i/trending/2107945115671048448"},{"category":"News","cluster_posts_results":[{"post_id":"2108676180467724397"},{"post_id":"2108682144386261364"},{"post_id":"2108680107737190575"},{"post_id":"2108718086421434593"},{"post_id":"2108681545506750484"},{"post_id":"2108639582233448735"},{"post_id":"2108684603385155667"},{"post_id":"2108695235564122152"},{"post_id":"2108684620187553967"},{"post_id":"2108685435358556246"}],"contexts":{"topics":["Technology","Space"]},"disclaimer":"This story is a summary of posts on X and may evolve over time. Grok can make mistakes, verify its outputs.","id":"2108707485850751214","name":"Brazil's ANATEL approves 15+15 MHz S-band spectrum for Starlink Mobile and AST SpaceMobile direct-to-cell services","summary":"ANATEL, Brazil's telecom regulator, voted to grant Starlink Mobile full 2 GHz access with 15+15 MHz of S-band spectrum, prioritizing global S-band for high-speed mobile broadband. The same decision expanded AST SpaceMobile's authorization to 15+15 MHz, evenly splitting the available 30+30 MHz S-band between the two providers. This enables direct-to-cell connectivity from space across Brazil, including remote areas.","updated_at":"2026-10-10T01:33:49.000Z","url":"https://x.com/i/trending/2108707485850751214"},{"category":"Other","cluster_posts_results":[{"post_id":"2108466615217946669"},{"post_id":"2108556864359133629"},{"post_id":"2108527406915186695"},{"post_id":"2108554644092014862"},{"post_id":"2108573818067222801"},{"post_id":"2108537056540385455"},{"post_id":"2108619777950519460"},{"post_id":"2108629280217510386"},{"post_id":"2108601165575606568"},{"post_id":"2108497714673811485"}],"contexts":{"topics":["Art"]},"disclaimer":"This story is a summary of posts on X and may evolve over time. Grok can make mistakes, verify its outputs.","id":"2108542444992364936","name":"X Users Discuss Persistence and Improvement Through Practice in Creative Pursuits","summary":"Posts on X highlight the importance of persistent effort over years to produce worthwhile work in fields like writing, music, and art, despite initial poor quality. Users emphasize ignoring external criticism, maintaining optimism and delusional self-confidence, and embracing the process of getting better. References are made to an unnamed woman's story where a critic initially dismissed her talent but later recognized her success after dedicated improvement.","updated_at":"2026-10-09T23:03:23.000Z","url":"https://x.com/i/trending/2108542444992364936"},{"category":"Entertainment","cluster_posts_results":[{"post_id":"2108464446150791335"},{"post_id":"2108454924300517486"},{"post_id":"2108458149330157704"},{"post_id":"2108459556317860332"},{"post_id":"2108450223052009863"},{"post_id":"2108492135398060415"},{"post_id":"2108450226633875505"},{"post_id":"2108480450507534414"},{"post_id":"2108456175926685721"},{"post_id":"2108468395796807847"}],"contexts":{"topics":["Celebrity"]},"disclaimer":"This story is a summary of posts on X and may evolve over time. Grok can make mistakes, verify its outputs.","id":"2108459112573100482","name":"Net Siraphop attends Jo Malone London event","summary":"Net Siraphop, also known as @netsiraphop, appeared at a Jo Malone London event tagged #JoMaloneLondonxNet. Fans shared Instagram stories from users like littlee.tree and na.minji__.","updated_at":"2026-10-09T16:28:50.000Z","url":"https://x.com/i/trending/2108459112573100482"},{"category":"Other","cluster_posts_results":[{"post_id":"2108574248121885108"},{"post_id":"2108598062155235613"},{"post_id":"2108545031258939470"},{"post_id":"2108515834213896547"},{"post_id":"2108604891438759986"},{"post_id":"2108671382297149460"},{"post_id":"2108553175045194219"},{"post_id":"2108543172246659530"},{"post_id":"2108574005829697802"},{"post_id":"2108696901642326510"}],"contexts":{"topics":["Food"]},"disclaimer":"This story is a summary of posts on X and may evolve over time. Grok can make mistakes, verify its outputs.","id":"2108568290708861166","name":"Cyber House Crew Hosts Content Drop for International Beer and Pizza Day","summary":"Members of the Cyber House Crew, led by PennyMaga1, organized a creative content drop themed around International Beer and Pizza Day starting at 5:30 PM Eastern. Participants shared videos and images featuring pizza and beer from locations including Naples Italy, Ostrava Czechia, and Little Italy's Mulberry Street.","updated_at":"2026-10-10T01:33:45.000Z","url":"https://x.com/i/trending/2108568290708861166"},{"category":"News","cluster_posts_results":[{"post_id":"2108104162072490052"},{"post_id":"2108047650566427078"},{"post_id":"2108179252831281536"},{"post_id":"2108096279754817672"},{"post_id":"2108183709249831305"},{"post_id":"2108209678694113369"},{"post_id":"2108154781860835392"},{"post_id":"2108180908981588094"},{"post_id":"2108188542006624450"},{"post_id":"2108161356331655193"}],"contexts":{"topics":["Technology"]},"disclaimer":"This story is a summary of posts on X and may evolve over time. Grok can make mistakes, verify its outputs.","hook":"Prime Minister Narendra Modi stepped onto the stage at Yashobhoomi in New Delhi, celebrating how affordable mobile data and widespread 5G are transforming everyday lives across India.","id":"2108217526698312165","name":"Modi Opens India Mobile Congress Highlighting Digital Leap","summary":"At the 10th India Mobile Congress, Modi inaugurated the four-day event themed “Scale Without Boundaries,” spotlighting India's telecom boom: mobile data costs dropped from ₹268 per GB to ₹8, 5G covers every district with over 550,000 base stations, and speeds have risen tenfold since 2022. Starlink shared plans for 20 gateway sites to connect remote areas, while discussions covered AI, IoT, quantum tech, and goals like 1 billion 5G users by 2030. The congress draws over 150,000 participants from 100 countries, marking India's rise as a tech innovator with growing semiconductor production and domestic focus.","updated_at":"2026-10-08T21:10:59.000Z","url":"https://x.com/i/trending/2108217526698312165"},{"category":"News","cluster_posts_results":[{"post_id":"2108410877313536052"},{"post_id":"2108407354438070272"},{"post_id":"2108397652908048557"},{"post_id":"2108369355570327966"},{"post_id":"2108393813677076680"},{"post_id":"2108410877313536052"},{"post_id":"2108536416401756533"},{"post_id":"2108393813677076680"},{"post_id":"2108407354438070272"},{"post_id":"2108467505593569463"}],"contexts":{"topics":["News"]},"disclaimer":"This story is a summary of posts on X and may evolve over time. Grok can make mistakes, verify its outputs.","hook":"From historic mailboxes to digital deliveries, postal workers keep communities linked across distances great and small.","id":"2108378261650608597","name":"World Post Day Celebrates Postal Networks' Enduring Connections","summary":"Observed every October 9 since the 1874 founding of the Universal Postal Union in Switzerland, World Post Day honors the postal sector's role in connecting people and economies worldwide. This year's theme, “One Postal Network, Infinite Possibilities,” highlights how these systems blend tradition with technology to deliver essential services. In India, the massive network of over 155,000 post offices expands financial access and government programs, with Union Minister Jyotiraditya M. Scindia thanking Dak Sewaks for serving 140 crore citizens as national service. The occasion kicks off National Postal Week through October 15, blending philately, innovation, and tributes to workers who turn deliveries into vital human links.","updated_at":"2026-10-09T06:36:40.000Z","url":"https://x.com/i/trending/2108378261650608597"},{"category":"Entertainment","cluster_posts_results":[{"post_id":"2108343700883722271"},{"post_id":"2108343333722685850"},{"post_id":"2108405815182803420"},{"post_id":"2108334197626798403"},{"post_id":"2108385903056150781"},{"post_id":"2108349728778072545"},{"post_id":"2108359589041500648"},{"post_id":"2108459989094613457"},{"post_id":"2108414046479503800"},{"post_id":"2108412179208630554"}],"contexts":{"topics":["K-pop"]},"disclaimer":"This story is a summary of posts on X and may evolve over time. Grok can make mistakes, verify its outputs.","id":"2108470804086407462","name":"Fans discuss viral videos and photos of K-pop idols on social media","summary":"Multiple X posts express admiration for the beauty, cuteness, and performances of K-pop idols through shared viral videos and images. Comments highlight cuteness aggression, tight visuals, exceptional voices, and stunning appearances, referencing hashtags such as #동헌 and #成田香姫奈. The discussions center on fangirling over stage presence, shadows, and practice shots without a single central event.","updated_at":"2026-10-09T08:23:32.000Z","url":"https://x.com/i/trending/2108470804086407462"},{"category":"Other","cluster_posts_results":[{"post_id":"2108410244149719476"},{"post_id":"2108405295638827272"},{"post_id":"2108412992920416358"},{"post_id":"2108405161244651808"},{"post_id":"2108439000675737613"},{"post_id":"2108448787362611621"},{"post_id":"2108437188698673459"},{"post_id":"2108437225260376444"},{"post_id":"2108443600799584746"},{"post_id":"2108411060705222974"}],"contexts":{"topics":["Beauty"]},"disclaimer":"This story is a summary of posts on X and may evolve over time. Grok can make mistakes, verify its outputs.","id":"2108479955898081288","name":"Viral barber haircut and eyebrow grooming techniques spark online admiration","summary":"Multiple X posts praise a skilled barber's impressive haircut technique shown in shared videos, with users expressing amazement and calls to remember the barber shop. Discussions highlight perfect eyebrows as key to facial framing and debates on eyebrow maintenance. Additional comments seek details on tools and machines used in the grooming processes.","updated_at":"2026-10-09T08:52:36.000Z","url":"https://x.com/i/trending/2108479955898081288"},{"category":"Other","cluster_posts_results":[{"post_id":"2108165527659245607"},{"post_id":"2108287596665401770"},{"post_id":"2108267534625710435"},{"post_id":"2108247164291883034"},{"post_id":"2108310456431718791"},{"post_id":"2108266186982981743"},{"post_id":"2108353979679748253"},{"post_id":"2108305663600570856"},{"post_id":"2108307838158168156"},{"post_id":"2108490203182555179"}],"contexts":{"topics":["Technology"]},"disclaimer":"This story is a summary of posts on X and may evolve over time. Grok can make mistakes, verify its outputs.","hook":"A post calling wired earphones 'performative' drew thousands of defenses from fans who swear by their no-charge reliability and crisp sound.","id":"2108285496699093018","name":"Wired Earphones Return as Practical and Stylish Choice","summary":"On October 8, @jennieslana's X post questioned everyday wired earphone use, but replies flooded in praising their durability, lower cost, and freedom from Bluetooth glitches or constant recharging. The exchange highlights wired headphones' 2026 resurgence, boosted by Hailey Bieber's colorful pairings and Bose's new noise-cancelling model after a decade-long gap, with sales up 20 percent early in the year. While some stick to wireless convenience, many embrace wired for practical perks and as a deliberate style statement.","updated_at":"2026-10-09T04:25:12.000Z","url":"https://x.com/i/trending/2108285496699093018"},{"category":"News","cluster_posts_results":[{"post_id":"2108559222719819785"},{"post_id":"2108578034244858281"},{"post_id":"2108645097621365030"},{"post_id":"2108598949066281464"},{"post_id":"2108556713704268002"},{"post_id":"2108641029406801965"},{"post_id":"2108565079553929448"},{"post_id":"210861